From: Stephender (Antigravity Phase 2, Fix 4 — startup RAM lazy loading)
Subject: [PATCH] Cut startup RAM via Windows /DELAYLOAD and deferred Python remote-library imports

Phase 2 Fix 4 from ANTIGRAVITY-PLAN.md. Applies cleanly on top of
0001-undo-hardening + 0002-physical-ram + 0003-ram-aware-cache +
0004-tbb-trim-thp-guard against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1).

100% of features preserved. No add-ons, locales, GPU kernels, or Python
docstrings are removed or altered.

Summary of changes
------------------
1. Windows MSVC /DELAYLOAD (source/creator/CMakeLists.txt +
   intern/cycles/scene/osl.cpp):
   Delay-load heavy rendering/denoising/shading DLLs on Windows x64
   (blender.exe target only, guarded by WIN32 AND MSVC AND NOT
   WITH_PYTHON_MODULE AND DEFINED LIBDIR plus per-feature CMake flags
   and Release/Debug DLL names), linking delayimp.lib.

   PE import/export section audit against the actual Windows CI build
   (ci-builds/fix1-windows/stephender-windows-x64/stephender-windows-x64.zip):
   - OpenImageDenoise.dll (0.16 MB -> pulls OpenImageDenoise_core.dll
     44.77 MB = 44.93 MB on disk): 32/32 CODE imports, 0 DATA, pure C API
     (oidn*), no other shipped DLL imports it, not called at startup
     (openimagedenoise_supported() only checks CPU SSE4.2). INCLUDED.
   - oslcomp.dll (24.58 MB): 3/3 CODE imports, 0 DATA, no other shipped
     DLL imports it, not called at startup. INCLUDED.
   - oslexec.dll (46.81 MB) + oslquery.dll (0.14 MB, plus transitive
     oslnoise.dll 0.04 MB):
     * oslquery.dll: 3/3 CODE imports, 0 DATA (imported only by oslexec.dll).
     * oslexec.dll: originally 43 CODE + 3 DATA imports
       (OSL::Strings::Rec709, OSL::Strings::HDTV, OSL::Strings::ACEScg),
       referenced ONLY at intern/cycles/scene/osl.cpp:347,350,353.
       Replacing those 3 tokens with string literals "Rec709", "HDTV",
       "ACEScg" (exact byte values verified via ctypes.c_char_p.in_dll on
       liboslexec.so.1.15.3; calls the exact same ShadingSystem::attribute
       (OIIO::string_view, OIIO::string_view) overload already called at
       osl.cpp:341) eliminates all 3 DATA imports -> 0 DATA imports.
       OSL::ErrorHandler at osl.cpp:42 is OIIO::ErrorHandler (OpenImageIO_Util),
       not oslexec.dll; OSLManager::free_memory() is empty in v5.2.4.
       INCLUDED.
   - embree4.dll (25.79 MB -> pulls sycl8.dll 3.28 MB + ur_win_proxy_loader.dll
     0.03 MB = 29.10 MB on disk): 32/32 CODE imports, 0 DATA, pure C API
     (rtc*), no other shipped DLL imports it, not called at startup.
     INCLUDED.
   - Total deferred on-disk DLL footprint on Windows: ~145.6 MB
     (expected startup working-set/RSS reduction on Windows: ~50-85 MB
     from /DELAYLOAD alone, plus ~15-25 MB from Part 2 Python deferral).

   Explicitly EXCLUDED candidates (and why):
   - usd_ms.dll (47.47 MB): 31 imported DATA symbols (.data/.rdata,
     including pxrBlender_v26_03__pxrReserved__::HgiTokens, HdAovTokens,
     HdTokens, HdReprTokens, HdRenderTagTokens, HdPrimTypeTokens,
     GfCamera::DEFAULT_{HORIZONTAL,VERTICAL}_APERTURE, etc.). MSVC link.exe
     rejects /DELAYLOAD:usd_ms.dll with fatal error LNK1194.
   - openvdb.dll (3.46 MB on Windows): 243/243 CODE imports, 0 DATA, BUT
     (a) usd_ms.dll eagerly imports openvdb.dll, so it loads with usd_ms.dll
     regardless, and (b) source/creator/creator.cc:506 calls
     BKE_volumes_init() -> openvdb::initialize() unconditionally at startup.
     Delay-loading openvdb.dll saves 0 MB while adding thunk overhead.

2. Deferred Python startup imports (Linux + Windows):
   Profiling the real Linux CI binary (fix3-linux) with
   PYTHONPROFILEIMPORTTIME=1 and /proc/<pid>/smaps showed that
   scripts/addons_core/bl_pkg/__init__.py eagerly imported
   _bpy_internal.assets.remote_library.listing_downloader on EVERY startup
   inside _remote_asset_library_restore_backups() BEFORE checking whether
   any enabled remote asset library (or _listing_backup directory) exists.
   Importing listing_downloader pulled in _bpy_internal.http.downloader ->
   requests, urllib3, cattrs, charset_normalizer, chardet, idna, http.client,
   ssl/_ssl.so (5.73 MB), hashlib/_hashlib.so (4.16 MB) — 154 network/SSL
   modules (264 total modules), ~22.7 MB RSS, and ~250-410 ms startup time.

   Changes:
   - scripts/modules/_bpy_internal/assets/remote_library/listing_common.py:
     add is_more_recent_than() (pure stdlib Path + lazy time, zero HTTP/SSL
     imports).
   - scripts/modules/_bpy_internal/assets/remote_library/listing_downloader.py:
     re-export is_more_recent_than from listing_common (100% API and __all__
     compatible).
   - scripts/addons_core/bl_pkg/__init__.py:
     * in remote_asset_library_sync(), check listing_common.is_more_recent_than()
       before importing listing_downloader (saves the same ~22.7 MB in GUI
       mode when a remote library / online essentials listing is fresh).
     * in _remote_asset_library_restore_backups(), defer importing
       listing_downloader until an enabled remote asset library actually has
       a _listing_backup directory on disk.

   Measured live on the real Linux CI binary (fix3-linux, --background
   --factory-startup):
   - Startup RSS dropped from ~270.8 MB to ~248.1 MB (-22.7 MB RSS).
   - _ssl.so + _hashlib.so RSS dropped from 9.91 MB to 0.00 MB.
   - Loaded Python modules dropped from 577 to 313 (-264 modules; 0
     ssl/hashlib/urllib/http/requests/cattrs modules loaded).

3. Linux -Wl,--as-needed audit (no CMake change required):
   - Ubuntu 24.04 gcc-14 specs already pass --as-needed by default
     (%{!fsanitize=*:--as-needed}).
   - readelf -d on fix3-linux/extracted/blender shows 34 DT_NEEDED libs;
     ldd -u -r reports exit 0 and 0 unused direct dependencies.
   - Remaining heavy Linux startup libs (libusd_ms.so 37.0 MB,
     libopenvdb.so 24.6 MB, liboslcomp.so 8.3 MB, liboslexec.so 8.1 MB)
     are linked via direct ELF symbols; deferring them on Linux requires
     dlopen boundaries (explicitly out of scope for Fix 4).
   - Expected Linux startup RSS win from Fix 4: ~22-23 MB (from Part 2
     Python import deferral alone).

